WEBVTT

00:00:03.084 --> 00:00:06.129
Woman: Up. Get up!

00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:27.275
Dudley: Wake up, cousin!
We're going to the zoo!

00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:43.708
Petunia: Here comes the birthday boy.
Vernon: Happy birthday, son.

00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:48.713
Cook breakfast.
And try not to burn anything.

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:53.927
- Yes, aunt Petunia.
- I want everything to be perfect...

00:00:54.135 --> 00:00:57.055
For my Dudley's special day!

00:00:57.222 --> 00:01:02.227
- Hurry up! Bring my coffee, boy.
- Yes, uncle Vernon.

00:01:03.478 --> 00:01:06.564
Petunia:
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:12.237
- How many are there?
- 36. Counted them myself.

00:01:12.487 --> 00:01:15.698
36?! But last year I had 37!

00:01:15.907 --> 00:01:19.744
- But some are bigger than last year's.
- I don't care!

00:01:19.994 --> 00:01:22.497
This is what we're going to do.

00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:27.085
We're going to buy you two
new presents. How's that, pumpkin?

00:01:29.045 --> 00:01:34.384
Petunia: It should be a lovely day
at the 200. I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:37.971 --> 00:01:39.764
I'm warning you now, boy.

00:01:40.014 --> 00:01:43.518
Any funny business, any at all...

00:01:43.726 --> 00:01:46.771
And you won't have
any meals for a week.

00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:58.867
Dudley: Make it move.

00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:03.246
Move!

00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:05.957
- Move!
- He's asleep!

00:02:06.124 --> 00:02:08.710
He's boring.

00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:16.634
Sorry about him. He doesn't understand
what it's like, lying there...

00:02:17.093 --> 00:02:20.889
Watching people press
their ugly faces in on you.

00:02:23.641 --> 00:02:26.311
Can you hear me?

00:02:28.813 --> 00:02:32.817
It's just, I've never talked
to a snake before.

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:34.736
Do you...?

00:02:34.944 --> 00:02:39.073
Do you talk to people often?

00:02:40.158 --> 00:02:43.494
You're from Burma, aren't you?
Was it nice there?

00:02:43.661 --> 00:02:45.997
Do you miss your family?

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:53.588
I see. That's me as well.
I never knew my parents either.

00:02:53.796 --> 00:02:58.801
Mummy, dad, you won't believe
what this snake is doing!

00:03:24.118 --> 00:03:25.536
Anytime.

00:03:28.873 --> 00:03:30.792
Man: Snake!

00:03:46.224 --> 00:03:49.602
Mum! Mummy! Help me!

00:03:49.852 --> 00:03:52.981
My darling boy!
How did you get in there?

00:03:53.481 --> 00:03:58.569
Who did this? How did you get
in there? Is there a snake?

00:04:03.408 --> 00:04:08.746
It's all right, sweetheart.
We'll get you out of these cold clothes.

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:13.418
- What happened?
- I swear, I don't know!

00:04:13.626 --> 00:04:17.505
The glass was there
and then it was gone, like magic.

00:04:21.926 --> 00:04:24.721
There's no such thing as magic.

00:05:01.466 --> 00:05:04.177
Vernon:
Marge is ill. Ate a funny whelk.
